==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|堅}}

===Etymology===
The word 堅い have been derived from ancient Japanese origin かたし (katashi: “hard”) and applied the meaning of Chinese letter 堅 that means keeping its physical shape or behaviour by its excellent quality.

===Adjective===
{{ja-adj|kk|decl=i|hira=かたい|rom=katai}}

# Keeping one's behaviour unchanged by their excellent quality; [[firm]]{{attention|ja|this definition line is incomprehensible}}
#: 彼女の結婚への意思は'''堅かった'''。
#:: かのじょのけっこんへのいしはかたかった。
#:: ''Kanojo no kekkon heno ishi ha '''katakatta'''.''
#:: Her will for marriage was so firm.
# Keeping one's behaviour by their excellent quality; [[trustful]]; [[strict]]{{attention|ja|this definition line is incomprehensible}}
#: その僧侶は'''堅い'''行いをする。
#:: そのそうりょは'''かたい'''おこないをする。
#:: ''Sono sōryo ha '''katai''' okonai wo suru.''
#:: The behaviour of the priest is '''trustful'''.
# Leading a [[serious]] situation{{attention|ja|this definition line is incomprehensible}}
#: '''堅い'''話はそのへんにして...
#:: '''かたい'''はなしはそのへんにして...
#:: '''''Katai''' hanashi ha sonohen ni shite...''

